1. length()
• Purpose: Returns the total number of characters in a string.
eg: String s = "Java";
    System.out.println(s.length());

2. charAt()
• Purpose: Returns the single character located at a specified index position.
  eg: String s = "Java";
      System.out.println(s.charAt(1));

3. toUpperCase()
• Purpose: Converts all characters in a string into uppercase letters.
  eg: String s = "java";
      System.out.println(s.toUpperCase());


6. equalsIgnoreCase()

Compares Strings without considering uppercase or lowercase differences.

java

String a="JAVA";

String b "java";

System.out.println(a.equalsIgnoreCase(b));

Output: true

7. contains()

checks whether a String contains a particular sequence of characters.

Java

Strings "Java Programming";

System.out.println(s.contains("Java"));

output: "true"

8. substring()

• Purpose: Extracts a part of a String based on start and end index positions.
• Code:
java
String s = "Programming";
System.out.println(s.substring(0, 4));

• Output: Prog


9. replace()

• Purpose: Replaces specified characters or character sequences with new ones.
• Code:
java
String s = "Java";
System.out.println(s.replace('a', 'o'));

• Output: Jovo


10. trim()

• Purpose: Removes leading (beginning) and trailing (ending) spaces from a string.
• Example (continuing the pattern cut off at the bottom of the screen):
java
String s = "  Java  ";
System.out.println(s.trim());
Use code with caution.
• Output: Java (without the extra spaces around it).g.
